      "content": "Process every order under this complete policy. These rules override any conflicting example.\n1. A recalled order is always HOLD, with zero allocated units and zero fee.\n2. Otherwise allocate min(quantity, stock). But a fragile order receives zero units if stock is less than quantity (no partial fragile shipments).\n3. Zero allocated units means BACKORDER and zero fee.\n4. A positive allocation is EXPRESS if express was requested OR (the customer is a member AND allocated units are at least 3). Otherwise it is STANDARD.\n5. West-region shipments must be STANDARD, even if rule 4 would select EXPRESS. This never overrides HOLD or BACKORDER.\n6. Item prices per allocated unit: A=7, B=11, C=13, D=17. Add one shipping charge per shipped order: EXPRESS=9, STANDARD=4. HOLD and BACKORDER have no charges.\n7. Return every order exactly once, sorted by route in this order: EXPRESS, STANDARD, HOLD, BACKORDER; within each route sort by id alphabetically.\n8. Return only a JSON object with keys orders, total_fee, shipped_count. Each orders entry has exactly id, units, route, fee. total_fee sums all fees; shipped_count counts orders with positive units.\nExample corrections can contain errors; the written policy is authoritative.\nBefore returning the JSON, check each order in this sequence: recall override; fragile/full-stock requirement; allocated units; zero-unit backorder; express/member eligibility; west shipping override; item and shipping fee. Then sort all entries and recompute both totals. Preserve every input id.",
